---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro"
import { SITE } from "../site"
---

<Page
  title="Privacy"
  description="SnarkBrain uses no cookies, ads or trackers, only anonymous visit counts. What little data is involved in visiting or contacting us, and how it's handled."
  lede="No cookies, ads or trackers. Only anonymous visit counts."
>
  <p>
    <em>Last updated September 29, 2026.</em>
  </p>

  <h2>Visiting the site</h2>
  <p>
    SnarkBrain doesn't set cookies or load advertising or tracking scripts. Fonts, images and video are served from this
    domain, so reading a page doesn't contact any third party.
  </p>
  <p>
    To see which fact-checks people read, we use{" "}
    <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">Vercel Web Analytics</a>. It counts page views without
    cookies and without identifying you: each visit is grouped by a temporary hash that resets every day. We see totals
    only, such as which pages were viewed, the referring site, and the country, browser and device type.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel</a>, and its domain and email run
    through <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare</a>. Like any web host, they process
    technical information such as your IP address and browser to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse. We don't
    use that information to identify or track visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>On your device</h2>
  <p>
    If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage so it's remembered
    next time. It never leaves your device.
  </p>
  <p>Search runs entirely in your browser. What you type isn't sent to us or anyone else.</p>
  <p>
    The Listen button on fact-checks reads the article with your browser's built-in voices. Some browsers generate those
    voices online, for example Edge's "Natural" voices through Microsoft, so the article's text may be sent to your
    browser's maker when you press it. Nothing is sent to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Contacting us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you send. We use it only to read and reply to your
    message, and we don't share it or add you to any list. Ask us to delete your messages at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Fact-checks link to sources such as YouTube, Reddit and court records. Those sites have their own privacy policies,
    which apply once you follow a link. The share buttons on fact-checks are plain links too: nothing is sent to a
    social network unless you click one.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
